# Parse Department of Health and Human Resources (DHHR) data for WV

| Key Details |
|-|
| Resolves #370 |
State: WV |
Site: DHHR |

## Notes
- This PR adjusts the wv/dhhr fetch script to also produce a `metadata.ndjson` file containing the fetched URI, so this can be passed along to the rest of the pipeline.
  - Since the DHHR data is updated weekly, I hope this is useful information.
- This PR then parses the fetched HTML data into NDJSON, using BeautifulSoup.
  - The HTML data consists of a date, followed by counties, and for each county a list of vaccine site opening hours and details. Vaccine sites may appear multiple times, on different dates. See https://dhhr.wv.gov/News/2021/Pages/COVID-19-Vaccination-Clinics-June-7-12,-2021.aspx for example.
  - The general strategy is to build up a mapping `site details -> opening dates -> list of opening hours for each date`. The output is not quite in the normalised format, but I'm leaving further date processing for the normalise step.
  - Minor concern: the HTML parsing is somewhat sensitive to the line breaks and formatting markup in the original document, and this page updates weekly. Open to suggestions on how to make this more robust. Otherwise I'll keep an eye on it and update the parser if necessary.

## Data sample

